  "content": {
    "title": "Our top 5 Kentucky Derby contenders as Run for the Roses 2026 nears",
    "text": "Updated March 30, 2026, 11:07 a.m. ETRenegade and Commandment take the top two spots after victories in key Kentucky Derby prep races Saturday.Paladin falls off the list after an injury suffered during training on Saturday.Renegade and Commandment both stamped themselves as top Kentucky Derby contenders over the weekend, but the biggest news may have been about a horse who’s off the Run for the Roses trail.Risen Star winner Paladin was injured Saturday during a workout at Payson Park and is off the Triple Crown trail, the Daily Racing Form reported.Trainer Chad Brown told DRF that Paladin suffered a non-displayed condylar fracture of his right front ankle, an injury that was detected after Saturday’s workout.Paladin, a son of Gun Runner, was 3 for 3 in his career after winning the Grade 2 Risen Star on Feb. 14 at Fair Grounds. He had been scheduled to make his final Kentucky Derby prep in Saturday’s Grade 1 Blue Grass at Keeneland.Renegade may have established himself as the Kentucky Derby favorite with a 4-length victory in Saturday’s $1.5 million, Grade 1 Arkansas Derby at Oaklawn Park.Commandment also boosted his resume with a nose victory over The Puma in the $1 million, Grade 1 Florida Derby at Gulfstream Park.Buy tickets here for Better Derby Betting eventThe final three major Kentucky Derby preps are set for this Saturday — the $1.25 million, Grade 1 Blue Grass, the $500,000, Grade 1 Santa Anita Derby and the $750,000, Grade 2 Wood Memorial at Aqueduct.With five weeks to go until the Kentucky Derby, here’s our ranking of the top five contenders:1. RenegadeOwners: Robert and Lawana Low; Repole Stable (Mike Repole).Trainer: Todd Pletcher.Jockey: Irad Ortiz Jr.Sire: Into Mischief.Road to Kentucky Derby points: 125 (No. 2). Career earnings: $1,031,500.Last race: Won Grade 1 Arkansas Derby on March 28 at Oaklawn Park.Likely next race: Grade 1 Kentucky Derby on May 2 at Churchill Downs. 2. CommandmentOwner: Wathnan Racing (Tamim bin Hamad Al Thani). Trainer: Brad Cox.Jockey: Flavien Prat.Sire: Into Mischief.Road to Kentucky Derby points: 150 (No. 1).Career earnings: $1,017,339.Last race: Won Grade 1 Florida Derby on March 28 at Gulfstream Park.Likely next race: Grade 1 Kentucky Derby on May 2 at Churchill Downs. 3. The PumaOwners: OGMA Investments LLC (Gustavo Delgado); JR Ranch (Ramiro Restrepo); High Step Racing LLC (Randy Guy, Joe Noble, Kevin Avera, Jim Ferreira, Todd Perry).Trainer: Gustavo Delgado.Jockey: Javier Castellano.Sire: Essential Quality.Road to Kentucky Derby points: 106 (No. 4).Career earnings: $442,280.Last race: Second in Grade 1 Florida Derby on March 28 at Gulfstream Park.Likely next race: Grade 1 Kentucky Derby on May 2 at Churchill Downs. 4. Class PresidentOwners: WinStar Farm LLC (Kenny Troutt); First Go Racing (Preston Troutt); China Horse Club Inc. (Kit-Har Ng).Trainer: Todd Pletcher.Jockey: John Velazquez.Sire: Uncle Mo.Road to Kentucky Derby points: 50 (No. 10).Career earnings: $593,700.Last race: Won Grade 2 Rebel on March 1 at Oaklawn Park.Likely next race: Grade 1 Blue Grass on April 4 at Keeneland.5. Danon BourbonOwner: Danox Co. Ltd.Trainer: Manabu Ikezoe.Jockey: Atsuya Nishimura.Sire: Maxfield.Road to Kentucky Derby points: Qualified via Japan Road to the Kentucky Derby.Career earnings: $222,762.Last race: Won Fukuryu Stakes on March 28 at Nakayama Racecourse.Likely next race: Grade 1 Kentucky Derby on May 2 at Churchill Downs.Jason Frakes: 502-582-4046; jfrakes@courier-journal.com. Follow on X @KentuckyDerbyCJ.Our editors independently choose our recommendations. Some content is produced with paid support from a third party, however our editorial decisions remain independent. If you buy through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices and availability may change.Gambling involves risk. Please only gamble with funds that you can comfortably afford to lose. While we do our utmost to offer good advice and information we cannot be held responsible for any loss 